cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the exact release and, for any computation, the campaign document it used."
type: software
title: "Polyhedraproof: a checked SAT pipeline for twelve pairwise-adjacent planar faces"
authors:
  - family-names: Pirozhkov
    given-names: Andrei
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-6901-7843"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23434449
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pirozhkov-andrei/polyhedraproof"
abstract: >-
  Whether a polyhedron with twelve pairwise adjacent planar faces exists is an open question;
  the tetrahedron and the Szilassi polyhedron are the only known polyhedra with every two
  faces adjacent. This software encodes, as 59 CNF formulas, a necessary condition for such a
  polyhedron under the accompanying article's surface and face-intersection hypotheses.
  Given the article's reduction, checked refutations of all 59 formulas would prove
  nonexistence in that class. The pipeline has every refuted case checked by the verified
  LRAT checker cake_lpr. A pilot computation refuted the formulas of maps 1 and 2 in a
  rehearsal campaign; this release does not include, and does not claim, the completed
  computation.
keywords:
  - polyhedra
  - oriented matroids
  - SAT
  - LRAT
  - formal verification
# doi: the concept DOI of the software on Zenodo, which resolves to its latest version
# (docs/RELEASE.md, "Publishing"); the article's arXiv identifier goes below once it has one.
